# Mycelia Interactive — Agent Rules (`.cursor/agents.mdc`)

This file is for the **Mycelia Interactive** company website project only.
It is distinct from, and does not affect, the `.cursor/agents.mdc` in the **KAIA Wrapper** project, which remains permanently read-only and must never be written to or edited from this or any other session.

Root [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) remains immutable unless Jeremy directs otherwise. Where this file and root `AGENTS.md` differ on **commit/push vs deploy**, follow this file: commit/push are automated session hygiene; **production deploy stays approval-gated**.

## Project overview

**Mycelia Interactive LLC** company website ([myceliainteractive.com](https://www.myceliainteractive.com)).

### Actual stack (from this repo — do not assume other Mycelia projects)

| Layer | In use |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js **16.2.x** (App Router), `output: "export"` static export |
| UI | React **19.2.x**, Tailwind CSS **v4**, Framer Motion, `clsx` / `tailwind-merge` |
| Tooling | TypeScript 5.9, ESLint 9 + `eslint-config-next`, Vitest, React Compiler (`babel-plugin-react-compiler`) |
| Hosting | Cloudflare Workers via **Wrangler** (`wrangler.jsonc`); assets from `./out`; Worker entry `workers/signup-api.ts` (D1, AI binding, cron) |
| Package manager | **npm** (`package-lock.json`) |

There is no separate `typecheck` script. TypeScript is enforced via `next build` and, when needed, `npx tsc --noEmit`.

## Mandatory checks after every change

Run and pass before considering a change complete:

1. `npm run build`
2. `npm run lint`
3. `npx tsc --noEmit` (explicit typecheck; not a package.json script)
4. `npm test` (`vitest run`)

Also run any step-specific runtime/visual/mobile checks as appropriate.

## Version control policy (automated)

At the end of every working session:

1. Commit all appropriate local work to **`main`** with a clear message
2. Push to GitHub (`origin/main`) **only when Cloudflare Workers Builds will not live-deploy from that push** (see below)

No per-session approval is required for **commit**. Push requires checking the Workers Builds gate first.

Use GitHub CLI (`gh`) and git for repository operations. Branch is always **`main`** — never `master`.

### CRITICAL — push currently equals production deploy

This Worker is connected to **Cloudflare Workers Builds**, which builds and deploys on pushes to `main`. There is **no** GitHub Actions workflow in-repo; the live path is Cloudflare’s Git integration, not `npm run deploy` from the agent.

Until Workers Builds auto-deploy is disabled (or switched to a non-production branch), **do not treat `git push` as version-control-only**. Prefer local commit + report “ready to push” and wait for Jeremy, or push only after Jeremy confirms Workers Builds will not ship to production.

### Secrets gate before any automated push

Before enabling or performing automated push, confirm `.gitignore` excludes secrets:

- `.env*` is ignored except `.env.production` (public build-time `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` defaults only)
- Never commit `.env.local`, credentials, PEM keys, or API secrets
- Confirm repo visibility (public/private) before push; this repo may be public

Automated push removes the manual checkpoint that would otherwise catch an accidental secret commit — treat secret hygiene as mandatory.

## CDP — Deployment policy (NEVER auto-deploy)

**Never auto-deploy under any circumstance.**

Forbidden without Jeremy’s separate, explicit approval every time:

- `npm run deploy`
- `wrangler deploy` (any non–dry-run form)
- Cloudflare dashboard / Workers Builds “retry deploy” / promote
- Any MCP tool that publishes a Worker version to production
- Assuming “commit/push” is safe while Workers Builds is wired to `main`

Allowed without deploy approval:

- `npm run deploy:dry-run` (validation only; must not publish)
- Local `npm run build` / lint / test / typecheck
- Local commit (not push) when Workers Builds would ship on push

Dry-run checks (`npm run deploy:dry-run`) are allowed when validating Wrangler config as part of ordinary verification.

## Branch policy

- Work on **`main` only**
- Never create or use `master`
- Prefer `gh` for GitHub-facing operations (PRs, repo metadata, visibility checks)

## Standing constraints

- Never hardcode client names or sensitive business details into the codebase
- Mobile-first UI and proper error handling on all implementations
- Do not proceed from audit (Phase 1) to remediation (Phase 2) without Jeremy’s explicit approval of findings
